It is Thursday, half past five in the evening.
I am at the badminton club.
The sports hall is incredibly hot today.
I take my racket out of my backpack.
Lena and Timo are already waiting on the court.
Max is on holiday this week.
We are playing doubles and changing partners often today.
First, I am playing with Timo against Lena and another player.
The match is very tough and fast.
We run back and forth without a break.
Timo hits the ball very hard over the net.
Lena answers extremely quickly.
We are all sweating after just a few minutes.
Finally, the first set is over.
We sit down on the benches and take a deep breath.
"That was a great rally at the end!" says Lena.
"Yes, but I am completely exhausted," Timo answers and laughs.
I drink a lot of water.
The heat in the hall is extreme, but the evening is great fun.
